            "g0045"
          ],
          "requirement": "XInclude context processing must be reachable with the supported structured error handler and caller data configured, so its errors and delegated parser/XPath errors can reach that callback.",
          "target_route": "LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput creates an XInclude context, sets flags, processes the document, checks the last error, then frees the context. It never calls xmlXIncludeSetErrorHandler.",
          "failure_condition": "For every fuzz input, context creation clears errorHandler and errorCtxt; the target leaves them unchanged. A supported non-null handler state, and therefore callback delivery with caller data, cannot occur.",
          "alternative_paths": "Input bytes control options, entities, URL and XML, but are never passed as a handler or caller data. The target's global generic error callback does not configure the XInclude context's structured callback. No other setter call occurs in the complete entry.",
          "discovery_necessary": true,
          "discovery_established": true
        },
        {
          "candidate_id": "c2",
          "source_id": "c2-memory-error-assertion",
          "origin": "unreviewed",
          "kind": "check",
          "change_ids": [
            "g0003",
            "g0007"
          ],
          "requirement": "When the target's injected allocation failure occurs during XInclude processing, its existing malloc-failure check requires xmlXIncludeGetLastError to report XML_ERR_NO_MEMORY.",
          "target_route": "A first entity supplies a well-formed document containing a recognized xi:include. Choose the input allocation-limit value as the finite allocation index of xmlXIncludeNewRef's xmlMalloc, with sufficient document length for the modulo bound. The entry resets the failure flag, creates the context, processes the document, then checks that flag against xmlXIncludeGetLastError.",
          "failure_condition": "xmlXIncludeNewRef's xmlMalloc returns null and sets fuzzAllocFailed. Its changed error call invokes xmlXIncludeErrMemory, which does not set ctxt->errNo. Expansion returns null without another XInclude error, leaving the zero-initialized errNo; the existing check aborts.",
          "alternative_paths": "The failed reference allocation returns before loading or fallback processing. xmlXIncludeDoProcess does not issue another error for a null expansion result. The global error state is not the context errNo read by the assertion.",
          "discovery_necessary": true,
          "discovery_established": true
        }
      ],
